  "provenance": {
    "movie_menu": "The EU-only movie debugger owns its init/update/exit callbacks, private selection state, five read-only movie-ID/label records, eight label/display strings and Mode descriptor. The callbacks form the naturally aligned 0800C76C..0800C8B4 text run and access only their own work pointer at 020348C4. Native read-only data occupies 0812F680..0812F704 and the descriptor occupies 09F49A6C..09F49A7C, each following the effect debugger in original order. Ordinary C sections and compiler alignment reproduce all bytes and relocations. Both external ModeRequest consumers use the descriptor definition through movie_debug.h; the former gModeChkmov fixed-address alias named the same object.",
    "eu_task": "The EU-only 24-byte record at 09F59130 contains the exact task_frd_pooh ASCII name, the four existing front-prefix task callbacks and sizeof(UnkModeTestWork) value 0x170. The 14-byte original name lives at 08896644. US and JP have no corresponding record. The complete regional prefix now owns this native record and name in ordinary data and rodata sections, ending before task_lockon_0."
